 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t an objective, universally agreed “best” personal injury lawyer—fit depends on your case, and directory awards or ratings aren’t guarantees of results.\n\nA reasonable Pleasanton starting point is **Megan Burns at Mirador Law**: the Super Lawyers directory lists her for plaintiff-side personal injury and says she has received its designation from 2018–2026. **Paulo S. Kline Simon** is another local option listed for plaintiff-side personal injury; his firm is at 4615 First Street, Suite 230, Pleasanton.\n\nBefore choosing, speak with two or three attorneys and ask who will handle your case, their experience with your type of injury, how costs and contingency fees work, and whether they’ve handled cases with similar facts. Verify the attorney’s current license and disciplinary history through the **State Bar of California**. Super Lawyers listings are one source to consider, not an independent guarantee of quality.",
